WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.220
April 2020. Americans
were told to stay home,

2
00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:06.220
and malls went quiet.

3
00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:10.280
That month, the personal
saving rate hit 33 percent,

4
00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:13.060
up from 12.7 percent in March.

5
00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:17.450
Spending fell sharply, even though
most incomes were protected.

6
00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:20.240
So what makes a whole
country stop spending,

7
00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.380
even when pay hasn't changed?

8
00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:26.510
In this mission, you'll calculate
the marginal propensity to consume,

9
00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:30.460
and see why MPC plus MPS equals 1.

10
00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:33.610
Then you'll move the MPC
slider in a graph lab,

11
00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:35.420
predict what happens to the line,

12
00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:36.540
and test it.

13
00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:40.360
Your mission: find out what really
drives a country's spending.
